<Solution>
  <!--
    Sprint M3.2: the single, authoritative "build everything" solution for CI and local full-
    platform verification (`dotnet build Aovias.Platform.slnx`, `dotnet test Aovias.Platform.slnx`).
    Lists every cross-platform Aovias.* project in the repository — the full, exact output of a
    repo-wide `find *.csproj` scan, not a hand-curated subset — so this file cannot silently drift
    out of sync with what actually exists the way the per-area *.slnx files and the previously
    incomplete root Aovias.PublishingEngine.slnx had (see the M3.2 report for what was found and
    fixed in those). The five per-area *.slnx files (Aovias.Runtime.Agent.slnx, Aovias.Release.slnx,
    Aovias.CommandCenter.slnx, Aovias.Orchestration.slnx, Aovias.Publishing.slnx) and the root
    Aovias.PublishingEngine.slnx remain for focused area-scoped development; this file is additive,
    not a replacement.

    Sprint M4.1: Aovias.Bootstrap (Contracts/Core/Host + Core.Tests) is now in scope — Zero-Touch
    Environment Bootstrap — and is added to the Folder list below alongside every other area.

    Sprint M3.0 (Toolchain Restoration & Canonical Build Baseline): this file and
    `ComplianceServiceManager/ComplianceServiceManager.slnx` are the two canonical build entry
    points for the whole platform:
    - `Aovias.Platform.slnx` (this file) — every cross-platform (net10.0) production project:
      builds on any CI runner (Linux/Windows/macOS), no Desktop workload required.
    - `ComplianceServiceManager/ComplianceServiceManager.slnx` — the Windows/WPF leg
      (net10.0-windows, UseWPF): `ComplianceServiceManager` + `Aovias.DesignSystem`. Requires a
      Windows build agent with the .NET Desktop workload. Kept as a second, separate entry point
      rather than folded into this file for exactly the reason `Aovias.DesignSystem` was already
      excluded below.
    A repo-wide `find *.csproj` scan (M3.0) also found `AOVIAS.Infrastructure/tools/PublishAllServices` and
    `AOVIAS.Infrastructure/tools/PublishRuntimeAgent` — both net10.0, both previously in no solution at all — added to
    the new `/tools/` folder below.

    Deliberately excluded, with reason:
    - Aovias.DesignSystem - targets net10.0-windows with UseWPF=true; requires the Windows Desktop
      SDK workload, which most CI runners (and this sandbox) do not carry. Building it alongside
      the cross-platform server projects would make this file fail on any non-Windows build agent
      for a reason unrelated to the platform's own correctness. Covered instead by
      `ComplianceServiceManager.slnx` (see above).
  -->
  <Folder Name="/Aovias.Bootstrap/">
    <Project Path="Aovias.Bootstrap/src/Aovias.Bootstrap.Contracts/Aovias.Bootstrap.Contracts.csproj" />
    <Project Path="Aovias.Bootstrap/src/Aovias.Bootstrap.Core/Aovias.Bootstrap.Core.csproj" />
    <Project Path="Aovias.Bootstrap/src/Aovias.Bootstrap.Execution/Aovias.Bootstrap.Execution.csproj" />
    <Project Path="Aovias.Bootstrap/src/Aovias.Bootstrap.Host/Aovias.Bootstrap.Host.csproj" />
    <Project Path="Aovias.Bootstrap/tests/Aovias.Bootstrap.Core.Tests/Aovias.Bootstrap.Core.Tests.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <Folder Name="/Aovias.CommandCenter/">
